1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,067
The washer ate Jason's token and never
moved. Lucia heard it fall behind

2
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:07,000
the wall.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:12,688
Their payment was supposed to emerge
with a laundry sack. Its glass showed

4
00:00:12,688 --> 00:00:14,000
only dry cloth.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,667
Jason pushed another token toward the
slot. Lucia stopped him and checked

6
00:00:18,667 --> 00:00:21,000
the service diagram beneath the lid.

7
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,250
The washer had been disconnected. Its
coin chute fed a separate locker,

8
00:00:26,250 --> 00:00:28,000
inside the detergent cupboard.

9
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,789
Lucia opened the cupboard. The first
token had released a small tray, but

10
00:00:32,789 --> 00:00:35,000
the drawer stayed caught on fabric.

11
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:39,789
They eased the loose fabric from the
drawer's edge. The snag vanished, and

12
00:00:39,789 --> 00:00:42,000
their sealed payment slid into view.

13
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,529
Jason kept the second token. Whoever
arranged this delivery had expected

14
00:00:46,529 --> 00:00:49,000
them to keep feeding the machine.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,421
Lucia taped the spare token above the
slot. Underneath, she wrote: first

16
00:00:53,421 --> 00:00:56,000
load paid. They didn't offer a refund.
